<h2 id="s12">12. Support, Reporting Problems and Community</h2>
<p>12.1 UDAW is free software. <strong>There is no obligation on the Developer(s) to provide support, maintenance, updates, bug fixes, new features, compatibility, data recovery or any particular response time</strong>, and any help they do give is voluntary and given without warranty or liability.</p>
<p>12.2 <strong>Problems should be reported on our Discord channel.</strong> The Discord invite link is published in the <strong>README.md</strong> document that accompanies UDAW (and on the official UDAW repository page). When you report a problem, please give your UDAW version, your version of Windows, what you did step by step, what you expected, what happened instead, and any crash report that UDAW displayed.</p>
<p>12.3 Reporting a problem does not create any obligation to fix it, any warranty, or any contract between you and the Developer(s). Please be respectful in the community; the Developer(s) may remove content or users at their discretion.</p>
<h2 id="s13">13. Export Controls and Compliance</h2>
<p>You are responsible for complying with all export, import, sanctions and trade laws that apply to you and to your use of UDAW and its encryption and network components. You must not use UDAW if you are prohibited from doing so by law.</p>
<h2 id="s14">14. Trademarks</h2>
