<h2 id="s15">15. Term and Termination</h2>
<p>15.1 This agreement applies from the moment you first install or use UDAW and continues until terminated.</p>
<p>15.2 It ends automatically if you breach any of its terms. You may end it at any time by uninstalling UDAW and destroying all copies in your possession.</p>
<p>15.3 On termination you must stop using UDAW and stop distributing it and any UDAW Plug-ins. Sections 2.7 to 2.10, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17 and 18 survive termination, along with any other provision which by its nature is intended to survive.</p>
<h2 id="s16">16. Limitation Period and Waiver of Class Actions</h2>
<p>To the extent the law allows, any claim relating to UDAW must be started within one (1) year after the cause of the claim arose, or it is permanently barred. To the extent the law allows, you agree to bring claims only in your individual capacity and not as a plaintiff or class member in any class, collective or representative action.</p>
<h2 id="s17">17. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
<p>17.1 This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Victoria, Australia, and the federal laws of Australia that apply there, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules.</p>
<p>17.2 Subject to any rights you have under mandatory law in your country of residence, the courts of Victoria, Australia, have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of or relating to UDAW or this agreement.</p>
<p>17.3 Before starting any legal action you agree to first raise the issue with the Developer(s) through the community channel in section 12 and to make a good-faith attempt to resolve it informally for at least thirty (30) days.</p>
